SWEET T-289d log-only witnesses (patch 0209, PLAN-60FPS G-F20 climb 6): (1) with boot-arg sweetperf=1 one extra line per second with jobs: `SWEET PERF: jobhist jobs N lt100 .. lt250 .. lt500 .. lt1000 .. lt2000 .. lt4000 .. ge4000 ..` = histogram of submit -> completion seen per job (the duration of 0145, so it includes the <= 200 us poll latency); (2) every 30 s from the same tick the CMU_G3D PLL_G3D and PLL_G3D_L2 words are re-read (reads only, the window the boot print of 0203 mapped) and printed as `SWEET GPU: PLL g3d-t<sec> ...` / `g3dl2-t<sec>`. No register write, no behaviour change, no new boot-arg. Decides H2 (fixed cost per job: one narrow bucket) and H1 (PLL fallback after probe) of T-289d.
